<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21100] LFU: resume a device scan from a bookmark</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21100</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;A scan of a large target with &lt;tt&gt;llapi_scan_device()&lt;/tt&gt; can run for hours. If the application restarts, the scan has to start again from the beginning. OI Scrub and LFSCK keep a position so they can resume; an application running a scan needs the same, without touching the scrub's own state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Proposal (raised by Andreas):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The library generates an opaque, versioned bookmark of &lt;tt&gt;LLAPI_SCAN_BOOKMARK_SIZE&lt;/tt&gt; bytes and passes it to a new callback, &lt;tt&gt;lfsp_bookmark&lt;/tt&gt;, each time the scan finishes more of the target.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The application stores it and passes it back in &lt;tt&gt;lfsp_resume&lt;/tt&gt; to start the scan there after a restart.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The bookmark is the lowest chunk any worker still holds, so a resumed scan may deliver some objects again but misses none.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;It names the target (ldiskfs &lt;tt&gt;s_uuid&lt;/tt&gt;, ZFS pool and dataset guids) and the query (&lt;tt&gt;lfsp_want&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;LLAPI_SCAN_F_INTERNAL&lt;/tt&gt;). Another target is refused with &lt;tt&gt;-ESTALE&lt;/tt&gt;; another query or a damaged bookmark with &lt;tt&gt;-EINVAL&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;llapi_scan_namespace()&lt;/tt&gt; has no position to save and refuses both fields with &lt;tt&gt;-EOPNOTSUPP&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Follow-ups, not in the first patch:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lfs find --device --bookmark FILE&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The same for the in-kernel OSD scanner (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20720" title="LFU: in-kernel OSD scanner" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20720"&gt;LU-20720&lt;/a&gt;), through the dt iterator's &lt;tt&gt;store()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;load()&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
